(A website is a set of online pages that explains an organization and helps people contact it.) Tj T*
(It can build a clear online presence and answer common questions.) Tj T*
(Need: customers rely only on scattered social posts or repeated WhatsApp explanations. Users:) Tj T*
(companies, schools, hotels, restaurants, professionals, NGOs.) Tj T*
(Example: a fictional Arusha hotel lists rooms, location, services, gallery and inquiry) Tj T*
(contacts so guests can review details before messaging.) Tj T*
(JAYTRIX may provide home/about/services or products/contact/location pages, forms,) Tj T*
(WhatsApp/social links, gallery, news and content management where required.) Tj T*
(Benefits: clearer information, easier inquiries, better customer experience and an owned place) Tj T*
(to present the organization. Results depend on content and promotion.) Tj T*
(Signals: no website, outdated details, hard-to-find contacts, repeated questions. Ask: Who) Tj T*
(visits? What should they do? What content changes? Need forms, map, WhatsApp, languages? Who) Tj T*
(approves copy? Deadline?) Tj T*
(Say: We can organize your key information online and make it easier for customers to) Tj T*
(understand your services and contact you. May I ask how people find you now?) Tj T*
(Do not promise rankings, traffic, leads, copywriting, hosting, delivery date or features) Tj T*
(before scope is confirmed.) Tj T*
(Conversation: Rep: How do guests learn about rooms and location? Hotel: They ask us on) Tj T*
(WhatsApp. Rep: A website could present those details and direct guests to your preferred) Tj T*
(inquiry channel. Which information changes often? Rep: I will record the need and ask our team) Tj T*
(to confirm scope and cost.) Tj T*
